e":1216.6},{"lat":42.09528,"lng":1.758671,"ele":1215.2},{"lat":42.095268,"lng":1.758633,"ele":1215.2}]'::jsonb),
('wikiloc', '245693024', 'https://www.wikiloc.com/hiking-trails/alhama-de-granada-los-barracones-collado-donabuelo-la-maroma-salto-del-caballo-sl-a-124-245693024', 'Alhama de Granada: Los Barracones - Collado Donabuelo - La Maroma - Salto del Caballo (SL-A 124)', '{"en":"Alhama de Granada circular, snowy conditions","ca":"Circular Alhama de Granada, condicions de neu","es":"Circular Alhama de Granada, condiciones de nieve"}'::jsonb, 'Alhama de Granada: Los Barracones - Collado Donabuelo - La Maroma - Salto del Caballo (SL-A 124) Hiking trail in Corumbela, Andalucía (España). Download its GPS track and follow the itinerary on a map. This circular hike to La Maroma (2,069 m), also known as Pico Tejeda, explores the highest mountain in the province of Málaga and runs through the Natural Park of the Sierras of Tejeda, Almijara and Alhama. Walked under snowy winter conditions, the route offers a demanding but highly rewarding mountain experience, with wide panoramas and a strong alpine character. 
 
The hike starts at the Área Recreativa El Robledal and initially follows forest tracks toward Los Barracones, passing through extensive pine woodland mixed with native Mediterranean species. This lower section is gentle and well defined, allowing a steady warm-up before the terrain becomes more mountainous. 
 
From Los Barracones, the trail continues uphill to the Mirador del Contadero, a narrow and scenic viewpoint overlooking deep ravines and limestone cliffs. From here, the route gains height more noticeably, reaching the Collado del Selladero and shortly after the Collado Donabuelo, where snow cover typically becomes continuous in winter. These high passes mark the transition into open mountain terrain with increasingly expansive views. 
 
The ascent continues toward La Maroma, the highest point of the route. The summit area is a broad limestone plateau crowned by a large geodetic vertex. In winter, the open terrain can be very exposed, with cold temperatures and wind, but on clear days the views are exceptional, stretching across the surrounding sierras and, at times, as far as the Mediterranean Sea and Northern Africa. 
 
After leaving the summit via the official trail SL-A 124, the route crosses the dramatic Tajo Volaero, an exposed section with steep drops that requires special care when snow or ice is present. From there, the trail descends to Collado de la Lobera and continues to Puerto Lobera, also known as Salto del Caballo, an area that often retains snow and ice due to its shaded orientation. 
 
The return route leads to the Collado de Rojas, where the trail begins to re-enter more sheltered terrain. The final scenic highlight is the Mirador del Valle del Temple, offering beautiful views over the valley and surrounding mountain ranges before the descent back toward El Robledal. 
 
This winter ascent of La Maroma is a long and demanding hike, requiring good fitness and mountain experience. Due to the snow and occasional icy sections, spikes may be very helpful on the return, especially on shaded and compacted snow. Under these conditions, the route showcases the wild and alpine side of southern Spain’s highest mountain in Málaga.', '{"en":"This demanding circular hike to La Maroma (2,069 m), also known as Pico Tejeda, starts at Área Recreativa El Robledal. The initial section follows gentle forest tracks through pine woodlands towards Los Barracones, providing a steady warm-up.\n\nThe trail then gains height more noticeably, passing the Mirador del Contadero, Collado del Selladero, and Collado Donabuelo. These high passes lead into open mountain terrain with expansive views, often covered in snow during winter. The ascent culminates at La Maroma''s broad limestone plateau, offering a rewarding alpine experience over 17.5 km with 1080 m of elevation gain.","ca":"Aquesta exigent caminada circular a La Maroma (2.069 m), també coneguda com a Pico Tejeda, comença a l''Àrea Recreativa El Robledal. La secció inicial segueix pistes forestals suaus a través de boscos de pins cap a Los Barracones, proporcionant un escalfament constant.\n\nEl sender guanya alçada de manera més notable, passant pel Mirador del Contadero, el Collado del Selladero i el Collado Donabuelo. Aquests colls alts condueixen a terreny de muntanya obert amb vistes expansives, sovint cobertes de neu a l''hivern. L''ascens culmina a l''àmplia altiplà calcari de La Maroma, oferint una gratificant experiència alpina de 17.5 km amb 1080 m de desnivell.","es":"Esta exigente caminata circular a La Maroma (2.069 m), también conocida como Pico Tejeda, comienza en el Área Recreativa El Robledal. La sección inicial sigue suaves pistas forestales a través de pinares hacia Los Barracones, proporcionando un calentamiento constante.\n\nEl sendero luego gana altura de manera más notable, pasando por el Mirador del Contadero, el Collado del Selladero y el Collado Donabuelo. Estos puertos de montaña altos conducen a terreno de montaña abierto con vistas expansivas, a menudo cubiertas de nieve en invierno. El ascenso culmina en la amplia meseta caliza de La Maroma, ofreciendo una gratificante experiencia alpina de 17.5 km con 1080 m de desnivel."}'::jsonb, 'Cut_the_crap', 17477, 1080, 1080, 2063, 1084, 'moderate', 'loop', 19200, 31080, 3113, '2026-01-01', '2025-12', '[{"lat":36.929978,"lng":-3.996038,"ele":1096.7},{"lat":36.929924,"lng":-3.996135,"ele":1096.7},{"lat":36.929953,"lng":-3.996228,"ele":1096.7},{"lat":36.92993,"lng":-3.996279,"ele":1087.6},{"lat":36.929925,"lng":-3.996335,"ele":1087.4},{"lat":36.92989,"lng":-3.996382,"ele":1086.4},{"lat":36.929855,"lng":-3.996432,"ele":1086.3},{"lat":36.92982,"lng":-3.996469,"ele":1086.5},{"lat":36.929772,"lng":-3.996506,"ele":1086.6},{"lat":36.929734,"lng":-3.996548,"ele":1088.6},{"lat":36.929695,"lng":-3.996578,"ele":1089.3},{"lat":36.92966,"lng":-3.996629,"ele":1089.1},{"lat":36.929622,"lng":-3.996667,"ele":1088.8},{"lat":36.92958,"lng":-3.996713,"ele":1088.8},{"lat":36.929532,"lng":-3.99672,"ele":1090.8},{"lat":36.929574,"lng":-3.996761,"ele":1092.1},{"lat":36.929594,"lng":-3.996815,"ele":1090.3},{"lat":36.929596,"lng":-3.99688,"ele":1090.9},{"lat":36.929601,"lng":-3.996938,"ele":1090.9},{"lat":36.929589,"lng":-3.996994,"ele":1089.8},{"lat":36.929542,"lng":-3.996995,"ele":1089.4},{"lat":36.929489,"lng":-3.996999,"ele":1090.5},{"lat":36.929443,"lng":-3.997012,"ele":1090.8},{"lat":36.929397,"lng":-3.997021,"ele":1091.1},{"lat":36.92935,"lng":-3.997031,"ele":1092.4},{"lat":36.9293,"lng":-3.997032,"ele":1092.1},{"lat":36.929245,"lng":-3.997049,"ele":1091},{"lat":36.929199,"lng":-3.997063,"ele":1091.4},{"lat":36.929152,"lng":-3.997077,"ele":1091.4},{"lat":36.929107,"lng":-3.997081,"ele":1092.3},{"lat":36.929071,"lng":-3.997118,"ele":1093.3},{"lat":36.929037,"lng":-3.997159,"ele":1093.3},{"lat":36.928997,"lng":-3.99720